From: Myghi63 <myghi63@disroot.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:15:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] bootanimation: Flag every part 'p' so boot exit cuts it

Every part is flagged 'c' (play until complete), so when boot finishes
(service.bootanim.exit=1) the looping part still finishes its current cycle
and the outro plays fully on top of an already-booted system. With 'p' the
animation breaks as soon as boot completes.

Flagging the description keeps crDroid's own generator, so the frames still
match the device resolution bucket; the previous 16.0 approach (shipping a
patched bootanimation.zip and pointing TARGET_BOOTANIMATION at it) had to
guess that bucket.
---
 prebuilt/bootanimation/desc.txt | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/prebuilt/bootanimation/desc.txt b/prebuilt/bootanimation/desc.txt
index 4aecc8e..f51178b 100644
--- a/prebuilt/bootanimation/desc.txt
+++ b/prebuilt/bootanimation/desc.txt
@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
-c 1 0 part0
-c 0 0 part1
-c 1 0 part2
+p 1 0 part0
+p 0 0 part1
+p 1 0 part2
--
2.56.0
